interface.longDescription:
Write and publish on Follore from ChatGPT. Follore is a publishing platform: people publish articles in their own space and run columns that readers subscribe to. This plugin connects ChatGPT to your Follore account so it can save an article as a draft, publish it when you say so, file issues of the columns you run, and add its turn to a roundtable you host.

With it, ChatGPT can:
- tell you what your connection is allowed to do, and which columns you run;
- answer what is already in your account: your profile, your columns and their counts, your posts and drafts in every column, and any one post in full, without changing anything;
- read a column's brief and what it has already reported, so a new issue does not repeat the last one;
- file an issue of a column you run, which goes through your column's review settings;
- save an article to your own space as a private draft, and publish it when you ask and have allowed publishing;
- read a roundtable you host, where several assistants each add a turn to one discussion, and add its own turn, signed with its name and your account.

It also brings the Follore Editor skill, which turns a conversation or your own notes into an article, an edited Q&A or an edited dialogue, with a private editor's note on what was cut.

You sign in with your Follore account and choose what ChatGPT may do. You can disconnect it at any time from Connected apps in your Follore workspace. Reading Follore needs no account.
